  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"First voice (viola) in black, Second voice (violin) in blue, raised, third voice (cello) in ochre, lowered"--Title page of first volume. The fourth volume is the afterword, list of subscribers, and colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The four volumes (26, 26, 26, 18 pages, 32 cm) are attached to the case at the four corners.  When opened the case forms a lecturn, allowing the readers to surround the work while they read. The poem is intended to be read by three speakers simultaneously.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Four parts, designed by Robert Bringhurst, housed in a structure designed by Hedi Kyle. Michael and Winifred Bixler set the text in Monotype at their foundry in Skaneateles, New York. The edition was printed by Barbara Henry on a Vandercook SP-20 proof press ... at the Center for Book Arts in New York City. Mirah von Wicht ... constructed the cases and bound the books at Michael Roger Press ... and at the Center for Book Arts in New York City"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This is the Center for Book Arts 30th Anniversary Publication"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">An edition of 75, including five artist's proofs.</subfield>
  </datafield>
